{
  "rules": {
    "systems": "A vehicle is built from Systems. Each System has a Rating (what it does) and a track of boxes in the Healthy, Hurt, Injured and Broken bands, like a character’s pools.",
    "boxes": "Hull has boxes by size (Light 7, Medium 10, Heavy 15, Massive 20; Capital uses four Sections of 15). Power has Rating × 2 + 3 boxes. Every other System has Rating + 3 (at least 4).",
    "bands": "Broken is always 1 box. The rest split evenly over Healthy, Hurt and Injured, extras to Healthy first, then Hurt. Hurt −1 and Injured −2 to rolls that use that System; Broken takes it offline.",
    "cap": "Size caps the Rating of Hull, Weapons and Shields: Light 2, Medium 3, Heavy 4, Massive and Capital 5. Drive and Controls are not capped.",
    "deflect": "Vehicle Deflect = 10 + the pilot’s Acuity + the pilot’s tier bonus + Handling. Evade adds +2.",
    "hit_cap": "The gunner’s Hit Cap (5 + tier) limits the overage first; then the Scale Rule doubles or halves it; then Armor (and Shields) come off.",
    "damage": "A hit crosses Hull boxes. When a hit crosses 3 or more boxes, roll d20 on the System Hit table: that System takes the boxes instead. A vehicle without that System puts them on Hull. On a Capital vehicle, every hit rolls for the Section.",
    "effort": "Effort: commit Power boxes before rolling, +1 each, up to the Power Rating. A vehicle with no Power (muscle, wind or oars) commits Hull boxes, up to its size step (Light 1 … Capital 5).",
    "strain": "Strain: a weapon that draws on Power (every energy weapon, and every mech weapon) lists a strain cost and marks that many Power boxes each time it fires; moving at full Speed marks 1. In a round with neither, Power unmarks 2 boxes. Weapons with ammunition may list shots instead. Strain replaces Heat.",
    "crew": "Every crew member acts on their own initiative using their own Actions.",
    "scale": "Compare sizes, counting a character on foot as one size below Light. The Scale Rule resolves before Armor.",
    "scale_breaking": "Scale-Breaking weapons ignore the two-size floor and do half damage instead of none: the anti-tank rocket, the shaped charge, the boarding torpedo."
  },
